<.shell title="Banner" current={:banner}>
  <h1>Banner</h1>
  <p class="lead">Something true about the page until it changes. It stays.</p>

  <div class="example">
    <.banner kind={:success} title="Letters sent">
      <p><strong>12 tax credit letters created for 2025.</strong></p>
    </.banner>
    <.banner title="Important">
      <p>
        SAR Duty refreshes from D4H every night at 02:00. Changes made in D4H today show up tomorrow.
      </p>
    </.banner>
    <.banner kind={:warning} title="Hours changed">
      <p>This letter says 212h 30m. Attendance now adds up to 214h 00m.</p>
      <.button variant={:warning} size={:sm}>Replace letter</.button>
    </.banner>
    <.banner kind={:danger} title="Deleted in D4H">
      <p>SAR Duty saw it was gone on October 2, 2026.</p>
    </.banner>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Success: the result of a big action, kept on the page.</li>
    <li>Info, the default: something people should know about the whole page.</li>
    <li>Warning: a risk that isn't a problem yet.</li>
    <li>Danger: the page can't do its job until something changes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A quick result that can go away. Use a <a href={page_path(:toast)}>toast</a>.</li>
    <li>A problem with one field. Show the error on the field.</li>
    <li>
      A consequence right before an action. Use <a href={page_path(:warning_text)}>warning text</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    At the top of the page, under the header. One at a time. The icon follows the kind. Success
    is a status, danger an alert, and the others a labelled region.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.banner kind=&#123;:warning&#125; title="Hours changed"&gt;</code>, with paragraphs
    and an optional button inside. <code>kind</code>
    is <code>:info</code>, <code>:success</code>, <code>:warning</code>, or <code>:danger</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
